ps://www.discogs.com/artist/6146656-Beshken","type":"artist","urls":["https://twitter.com/Beshkenxo","https://soundcloud.com/beshkenmusic","https://www.facebook.com/BeshkenOfficial","https://www.instagram.com/beshkenxo/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/643319/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"643319","image":"https://i.discogs.com/w9fOh3ZwWxBmjutO4TQDC1f2MdE-HDxTLlctSINGSq8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:469/w:340/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY0MzMx/OS0xMjM0MTkzOTY5/LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/mnnQpmc5LEhagJhqFa8jhtugsCMat30m6XrrxEbVZQQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY0MzMx/OS0xMjM0MTkzOTY5/LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Brazilian singer.\r\nBorn April 29, 1941 in Rio de Janeiro. Died May 1, 2025.\r\n\r\nCaymmi was born in Rio de Janeiro, the daughter of [a406673] and Stella Maris. Her first appearance on record was on her father's album Acalanto. She married Venezuelan doctor Gilberto Aponte Paoli and moved there in 1959. She and her husband divorced in 1966, at which time she moved back to Rio. At this time she became involved with the Tropicalia movement; she became romantically involved with Gilberto Gil. She sang \"Saveiros\" at the IFIC song festival in 1966, and won first place despite boos from the crowd (who preferred Gal Costa's rendition of Gil's \"Minha Senhora\"). \r\n\r\nCaymmi became a controversial figure, not at home in the Tropicalia scene nor in the protest song movement. Only marginally successful, she found work singing in Portuguese language nightclubs outside of Brazil in South America. In the 1980s, she recorded several albums for EMI, and appeared in the 1983 documentary Bahia de Todos os Sambas. In the 1990s she became more successful in the mainstream with her album Bolero, which was her first of several gold albums. In 1995 and 1998 she was named Best Female Singer of the Year by the APCA. In 2010 French director Georges Gachot released a documentary film Rio Sonata about Nana Caymmi.\r\nSister of [a301764] and [a309844]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:643319","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Caymill","Caymmi","Caymmil","Caymmy","D. Caymmi","Dorival Caymmi","Kaymel","Kaymmi","Nana","Nana Caymi","Naná","Naná Caymmi","Nãna","Nãna Caymmi"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/643319-Nana-Caymmi","type":"artist","urls":["https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nana_Caymmi","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nana_Caymmi","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0147304/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6677/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6677","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:6677","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":6676,"name":"Nuron"},{"id":917809,"name":"Nurmad Jusat"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":537460,"name":"Naoyoshi Matsuyama"},{"active":true,"id":2483556,"name":"Masashi Kameda"},{"active":true,"id":4107729,"name":"遠藤"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/6677-Fugue","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6967716/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6967716","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:6967716","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/6967716-Ganjoid","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/77811/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"77811","image":"https://i.discogs.com/W_qZT8M8gFKCHXNqkMrr9HhbwRLqqY00AbFxH4-pY2o/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc3ODEx/LTE1MTM3MjM1Nzct/ODQ1My5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/wp4Ui4zbWrYokfTzwSW60m8tQm1piXcWGDApQRmM_AU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc3ODEx/LTE1MTM3MjM1Nzct/ODQ1My5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Reggae singer and songwriter Dennis Brown (born February 1, 195